          {
            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0017",
            "textSha256": "456c18cc07f2b778744ba07b88e0a12439eb70f2a3dab80c52fb3be79d22aef1"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "Today is the day birders talk about for years. We walk through the jungle and climb up trails next to the river, looking for the Guianan Cock-of-the-Rock, a bright orange bird so beautiful it seems unreal. You might also hear the strange call of the Capuchin Bird echoing through the trees. You will not forget this day.\n\nAccommodation at Zintete Lodge, all meals, guide and transfer included."
